{
  "openapi": "3.0.2",
  "info": {
    "title": "RabbitMQ Management HTTP API (queues, exchanges, bindings, publishing)",
    "version": "4.4.0",
    "description": "Written by hand from RabbitMQ's published reference, which is an HTML page and has no OpenAPI document (rabbitmq-server v4.4.0, deps/rabbitmq_management/priv/www/api/index.html, read 2026-11-01). Trimmed to the messaging objects a client works with: no users, permissions, policies, or node and definition endpoints. Response fields and the status and body of each error come from running those requests against the rabbitmq:4-management image (RabbitMQ 4.4.0), read 2026-11-01. STACKIT's own broker has not been probed; which versions it offers and what its credential roles allow is unknown."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://rabbitmq.example.invalid"
    }
  ],
